@startuml
title Hexagonal SCIM - Sequence Diagram (Aligned Presentation Theme)

scale 0.5
' Theme aligned with component diagram tones
skinparam backgroundColor #0D1117
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundCorner 12
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontColor #E6EDF3
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam ArrowColor #58A6FF
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.3
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #30363D
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #161B22
skinparam ParticipantFontColor #E6EDF3
skinparam LifelineBorderColor #4B5563
skinparam LifelineBackgroundColor #0F172A
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #1F2937
skinparam NoteBorderColor #374151
skinparam NoteFontColor #D1D5DB

actor "API Client" as Client #93C5FD
participant "UserControllerAdapter\n(hex-inbound-adapter-web)" as Controller #38BDF8
participant "CreateUserPort\n(hex-core port.in)" as CreatePort #818CF8
participant "GetUserPort\n(hex-core port.in)" as GetPort #818CF8
participant "UserService\n(hex-core)" as Service #C4B5FD
participant "UserRepositoryPort\n(hex-core port.out)" as RepoPort #A78BFA
participant "UserRepositoryAdapter\n(hex-outbound-adapter-db)" as RepoAdapter #34D399
participant "UserJpaRepository\n(Spring Data)" as JpaRepo #6EE7B7
database "PostgreSQL / H2" as Db #FCA5A5
participant "ApiExceptionHandlerAdapter" as ExHandler #38BDF8
participant "LegacyApiDeprecationProperties" as LegacyProps #22D3EE

== Flow 1: Create User (Versioned Endpoint) ==
Client -> Controller: POST /api/v1/users\n{email, displayName}
activate Controller
Controller -> CreatePort: create(email, displayName)
activate CreatePort
CreatePort -> Service: create(email, displayName)
activate Service
Service -> RepoPort: existsByEmail(email)
activate RepoPort
RepoPort -> RepoAdapter: existsByEmail(email)
activate RepoAdapter
RepoAdapter -> JpaRepo: existsByEmailIgnoreCase(email)
activate JpaRepo
JpaRepo -> Db: SELECT by email
Db --> JpaRepo: false
JpaRepo --> RepoAdapter: false
RepoAdapter --> RepoPort: false
deactivate JpaRepo
deactivate RepoAdapter
deactivate RepoPort

Service -> RepoPort: save(User)
activate RepoPort
RepoPort -> RepoAdapter: save(User)
activate RepoAdapter
RepoAdapter -> JpaRepo: save(UserEntity)
activate JpaRepo
JpaRepo -> Db: INSERT users
Db --> JpaRepo: persisted row
JpaRepo --> RepoAdapter: UserEntity(id,...)
RepoAdapter --> RepoPort: User(id,...)
RepoPort --> Service: User(id,...)
deactivate JpaRepo
deactivate RepoAdapter
deactivate RepoPort

Service --> CreatePort: User(id,...)
CreatePort --> Controller: User(id,...)
Controller --> Client: 201 Created\nUserResponse
deactivate Service
deactivate CreatePort
deactivate Controller

== Flow 2: Create User (Duplicate Email) ==
Client -> Controller: POST /api/v1/users\n{email already exists}
activate Controller
Controller -> CreatePort: create(email, displayName)
activate CreatePort
CreatePort -> Service: create(email, displayName)
activate Service
Service -> RepoPort: existsByEmail(email)
activate RepoPort
RepoPort -> RepoAdapter: existsByEmail(email)
activate RepoAdapter
RepoAdapter -> JpaRepo: existsByEmailIgnoreCase(email)
activate JpaRepo
JpaRepo -> Db: SELECT by email
Db --> JpaRepo: true
JpaRepo --> RepoAdapter: true
RepoAdapter --> RepoPort: true
RepoPort --> Service: true
deactivate JpaRepo
deactivate RepoAdapter
deactivate RepoPort

Service --> CreatePort: throws DuplicateUserException
CreatePort --> Controller: exception bubbles
Controller -> ExHandler: handleDuplicate(ex)
activate ExHandler
ExHandler --> Client: 409 Conflict\n{code: USER_ALREADY_EXISTS}
deactivate ExHandler
deactivate Service
deactivate CreatePort
deactivate Controller

== Flow 3: Get User (Legacy Endpoint + Deprecation Headers) ==
Client -> Controller: GET /api/users/{id}
activate Controller
Controller -> LegacyProps: read deprecation-value/sunset-date/successor-link
activate LegacyProps
LegacyProps --> Controller: header values
deactivate LegacyProps

note right of Controller
Adds response headers for legacy path:
- Deprecation
- Sunset
- Link
end note

Controller -> GetPort: getById(id)
activate GetPort
GetPort -> Service: getById(id)
activate Service
Service -> RepoPort: findById(id)
activate RepoPort
RepoPort -> RepoAdapter: findById(id)
activate RepoAdapter
RepoAdapter -> JpaRepo: findById(id)
activate JpaRepo
JpaRepo -> Db: SELECT users by id
Db --> JpaRepo: empty
JpaRepo --> RepoAdapter: Optional.empty
RepoAdapter --> RepoPort: Optional.empty
RepoPort --> Service: Optional.empty
deactivate JpaRepo
deactivate RepoAdapter
deactivate RepoPort

Service --> GetPort: throws UserNotFoundException
GetPort --> Controller: exception bubbles
Controller -> ExHandler: handleNotFound(ex)
activate ExHandler
ExHandler --> Client: 404 Not Found + legacy headers\n{code: USER_NOT_FOUND}
deactivate ExHandler
deactivate Service
deactivate GetPort
deactivate Controller

legend right
|= Tone |= Meaning |
|<#38BDF8> Inbound Web | Controller + exception handling |
|<#818CF8> Inbound Ports | Use-case interfaces |
|<#A78BFA> Outbound Port | Persistence abstraction |
|<#34D399> Outbound Adapter | DB adapter implementation |
|<#C4B5FD> Core | Business logic |
|<#FCA5A5> Data Store | PostgreSQL / H2 |
endlegend

@enduml